    "done_when": "Find which step of snapshot.candidates (reckon/crew/picker/snapshot.py) stalls under load. Change no repository file.\n\nThe pick-timings log ~/.config/reckon/crew/pick-timings.jsonl recorded a production pick on 2026-10-07 at 19:25:12Z (node review-of-stage-time-tests-answer-by-pair): latency 6,229 ms, snapshot_ms 5,693, jev_ms 492, state render 40. At that moment the fleet node was running two parallel 8-process test runs from a peer merge check. The one-pass fix already merged, so the six ledger scans are gone; something else inside the snapshot blocks under contention. The pick-latency census (~/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/pick-latency-census/) measured the snapshot only as a whole.\n\n1. In a scratch copy of the main tree under your report directory, time every step snapshot.candidates runs, per backend where it loops:\n   - the record pass;\n   - lane-document reads;\n   - budget and pace reads, including paid-lanes.json, budget_group and preflight;\n   - availability checks, including any subprocess or which lookups;\n   - the context-fit verdict;\n   - any filesystem walk or stat.\n   Run the real project reckon state with a stub Jev client, so nothing is spent.\n2. Measure idle, five picks, then under controlled load, five picks: a scratch CPU and I/O load generator that you start and stop yourself, roughly matching sixteen busy processes, with its pids listed and stopped by pid at the end. Report each step's median and maximum per condition.\n3. Name the steps whose time grows most under load, with call paths to file:line. For each, propose a change: caching with a stamp, moving out of the pick bound, or removing a subprocess. Give the expected saving, and mark which proposals would edit reckon/crew/dispatch.py or reckon/cli.py, both on hold for a module split.\n4. Negative control: inject a 1 s sleep into one step in the scratch copy, and show the timings attribute it to that step alone.\n\nDeliver report.md, timings.json and a small horizontal-bar figure of per-step idle and loaded medians, data-ink style, in your report directory. Leave no load generator running.",
